    "title": "Robert Irwin Reveals 'Zootopia 2' Voice Role During 'Dancing With The Stars' Disney Night! - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Just Jared ,\n1 days ago Robert Irwin is heading to the big screen!\nThe 21-year-old animal conservationist just revealed the big news that he has a voice role in the upcoming Zootopia 2 during this week’s Dancing With the Stars , which is celebrating the magic of Disney .\nKeep reading to find out more…\nDuring his pre-performance package, Robert and pro partner Witney Carson went to watch a screening of the upcoming Disney movie, and he shared that he is voicing a character!\nOf course, the character he is voicing is a koala, which are native to Robert ‘s home country of Australia. The name of the character? Robert Furwin!\nRobert is no stranger to voicing an animated character as he previously voiced Alfie in an episode of Bluey season two.\nThe news comes just over a month ahead of the movie’s theatrical release on November 26th.\nIn Zootopia 2 , detectives Judy Hopps (voiced by Ginnifer Goodwin ) and Nick Wilde (voiced by Jason Bateman ) find themselves on the twisting trail of a mysterious reptile who arrives in Zootopia and turns the mammal metropolis upside down. To crack the case, Judy and Nick must go undercover to unexpected new parts of town, where their growing partnership is tested like never before.\nCheck out the trailer here!\n2",
